    Odd-Leaf Balancing: The odd-element balancing rule if chunk.len() == 1 { hasher.update(&chunk[0]); hasher.update(&chunk[0]); } ensures deterministic hashing for odd counts (e.g., 9 events duplicating leaf 8 to form node 4, then propagating).

    Evidentiary Standard: Meets Federal Rules of Evidence FRE 902(13) (Certified Records Generated by an Electronic Process or System) and FRE 902(14) (Certified Data Copied from an Electronic Device, Storage Medium, or File) through deterministic canonicalization and asymmetric signature chaining.

Recommendations for Production Hardening

    Ring Buffer Watermarks: Under ultra-high packet rates on 100GbE CNS feeds, use BPF_RINGBUF_BUSY_BIT handling or tune bpf_ringbuf_output with notification sampling to prevent userland buffer overrun under burst conditions.

    CO-RE Struct Offset Generation: For the Postgres hook, replace raw pointer offsets ((char *)queryDesc + 8) with BPF_CORE_READ(queryDesc, sourceText) compiled with vmlinux.h / DWARF BTF generated from the target database binary.

    Async Batch Sealing: In the Rust daemon, process events using an mpsc queue and commit Merkle roots on either a time-based ticker (e.g., every 100ms) or an event-count threshold (e.g., every 10,000 events) to maintain real-time throughput without CPU starvation.
